  "differencesAndLimits": [
    {
      "subject": "Website version",
      "observation": "Live website is 14.199.0; the source reference remains pinned to 14.197.0. Neither source pin was advanced."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Deferred language",
      "observation": "Forge displays I Speak Their Language (Soldier) for the unselected language slot and marks Career In Progress. Its export has only Vaslorian selected; this is not a fourth granted language. The existing audited Grug deliberately retains one lawful deferred Soldier language."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Wrecking Ball distance/target labels",
      "observation": "Forge puts see below on target: distance Self, target Self; see below. Pinned Compendium puts it on distance: distance Self; see below, target Self. Movement and adjacent-enemy roll text are present; Salient must preserve source labels."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Experience",
      "observation": "The website sets XP to 16 when the editor level increases to two. This is reference-site behavior, not authorization for Salient to award campaign XP as a side effect of advancement."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Level definitions versus active grants",
      "observation": "Both files embed higher-level definitions and unselected options. Only class levels <= current level, the selected Berserker branch and actual nested selections establish active grants; Special Delivery is present as an option but was not selected."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Winded",
      "observation": "Rendered desktop Hero tab captured Stamina and Recovery Value but did not display winded threshold. Winded19 remains an independent pinned-source expectation rather than a Forge screenshot observation."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Scope",
      "observation": "These are actual Forge Steel UI exports and Forge Steel reimport/export comparisons. They do not implement or verify Salient import/export, campaign advancement, progression history, live resource reconciliation or table automation."
    }
